  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented voucher support for the invoicekit. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code for attempting to apply multiple vouchers.\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Enhanced with:\n   - **New `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function**:\n     - Applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice only (NOT_DRAFT error if not draft)\n     - Prevents multiple vouchers per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS error if one exists)\n     - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error otherwise)\n     - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n     - Returns immutable copy with voucher applied\n   \n   - **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` function**:\n     - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n     - Calculates voucher from `invoice.voucher?.amount` (defaults to 0)\n     - Total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped to 0)\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 Added 17 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Basic voucher application and storage\n   - Status validation (draft-only)\n   - Duplicate prevention\n   - Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer)\n   - invoiceTotals integration with various scenarios\n   - Edge cases (large vouchers, small amounts, clamping to zero)\n   - Property preservation through voucher application\n\n**All 166 tests pass**, including the 17 new voucher tests.",
